cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Vigía in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "Vigía: quality control for the datasets behind network intrusion detection models"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Garcilazo
    given-names: Joshua
    alias: Joshua203-byte
version: 1.0.3
date-released: 2026-10-09
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/Joshua203-byte/vigia-nids"
url: "https://pypi.org/project/vigia-nids/"
keywords:
  - intrusion detection
  - NIDS
  - dataset quality
  - data leakage
  - machine learning
  - security
abstract: >-
  Vigía audits the datasets used to train network intrusion detectors for
  defects that inflate evaluation metrics (duplicates, train/test leakage,
  shortcut columns, label noise), detects data poisoning, and monitors drift
  in production.
